  "query_preview": "..\nA westerly monsoon push is expected to continue bringing heavier\nshowers and thunderstorms to the Marianas, especially to Tinian and\nSaipan overnight. After, a convergence zone is expected to shift\nfarther south, bringing higher shower and thunder coverage to Guam\nand Rota Tuesday. Once TS Peilou (formerly Kujira) shoots to the\nnorth and away from the Marianas and another disturbance begins\nconsolidating northeast of Pohnpei, a diffusive southwesterly flow is\nexpected to develop across the region. This will allow a dry spell \nto return, lasting until at least the weekend.",
